findings.citation_text:
4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) keg cooler in banquet bar (mold/liquid); 
B) inside warmer in kitchen (food debris); 
C) soda syrup rack in dry storage (dried splash); and
D) floor fan in the kitchen (dust).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) drip tray of stove top burners (carbon buildup/splash); 
B) keg cooler in banquet bar (mold/liquid); 
C) bottom inside warmer in kitchen (food debris);  and
D) soda syrup rack in dry storage (dried splash). 
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) fryers - sides and bottom around legs (grease);
B) metal cart used at bar (general buildup);
C) inner surface of sprayer at dish area (buildup);  and
D) can opener base (general debris/buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) can opener - blade and crevice around blade (food debris & metal shavings);
B) knife left from previous evening (food debris) - taken to dish area during inspection;
C) pizza slicers and racks left from the previous evening (food debris) - taken to dish area during inspection;  and
D) baffle inside ice machine (mold).

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use for in-use equipment and utensils (e.g. can opener, slicer, etc.), to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) can opener blade (food debris & buildup in crevice around blade);
B) tongs at oven (grease);
C) cutting board and knife (food debris);   and
D) ice machine - baffle inside (mold).

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed and up to every 4hrs after continuous use for in-use equipment such as knives, cutting boards, tongs, can openers, etc.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) inside prep cooler - ledge beneath condenser (food debris);
B) pans for seasonings on cook line (debris buildup);
C) pizza oven - general surfaces on back/sides (dust);
D) stove top - drip tray (carbon/splash);
E) sprayer sink - surface of sprayer (black buildup) & handles/faucet (buildup);
F) dish machine - around door seals (grease/buildup);
G) inside warmer (food debris/splash);  and
H) handles/general surfaces of upright coolers and freezers (splash/buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
